nt at least to  two or three degrees rising in  temperature  and this species has only recently been  rediscovered hasn't it so  how rare is it and are there concerns  about safeguarding it  yes there are it is a rare species it's  threatened with extinction in the wild  due to deforestation  and you know we have to do our utmost to  to preserve  not only this species but other species  that may have potential for  securing the long-term sustainability of  this detector  and you said earlier that it tasted  really good are you able to describe the  taste at all  yeah i am it's it's absolutely  fantastic we we had very low  expectations  um based on our other experiences of  wild coffee but this has a natural  sweetness  it has a great complexity of uh in its  flavour profile  it's everything you'd expect in a great  cup of coffee very well done it's not  easy to explain a taste dr aaron davis  thanks very much indeed  that's everything from us for today on  the daily climate show tomorrow our  correspondent cordelia lynch speaks to  environmental activist erin brockovich  whose successful lawsuit against the  pacific gas and electric company  was turned into a hollywood hit starring  julia roberts  i am aaron brockovich and i am delighted  to be here with you at sky news today  and i have to give you a shout out  because i am damn proud of you  taking on the conversation of climate of  water of this planet of its future  putting it out there so people know  so people can learn that's at the same  time tomorrow here on sky news  see you then  you

